# Git hook scripts must always use LF line endings, regardless of each
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting - a CRLF-mangled shebang line
# breaks the shell's ability to run the file at all. Without this, a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the common Windows default)
# would silently corrupt githooks/pre-push on checkout.
githooks/* text eol=lf
